description = "Experimental Xbox 360 core based on Xenia Edge. The graphics backend is chosen automatically: Vulkan on Linux, under Wine/Proton, and on AMD GPUs (xenia's D3D12 path is broken on AMD, and vkd3d-proton cannot translate its transfer shaders); Direct3D 12 elsewhere on Windows when the bundled D3D12 runtime is present. Override it with the GPU Backend option only if the automatic choice is wrong. Three layers of configuration are available - core options, xenia's own config file, and title-specific memory patches - documented in docs/libretro-configuration.md. GOD-format games launch via the extension-less package header file; disable 'Filter by supported extensions' to browse them."

notes = "No bundled system files are required; Xbox 360 games load directly.|(Controller) A standard Xbox 360/One pad maps 1:1 with no remapping needed.|(Controller) The release ships config/Xenia Edge/Xenia Edge.cfg - merge it into your RetroArch config folder. It pins input_player1..4_analog_dpad_mode to \"0\" so the left stick does not double as the d-pad, which otherwise scrolls menus while you walk. EmuVR forces that setting to \"1\" on all cores, so the file matters most there. A core has no API to change this - it is a frontend input setting.|(Config) Do not put commented-out settings in that file. RetroArch rewrites override files on exit when config_save_on_exit is on, and a commented line can come back uncommented - that once reactivated a video driver that did not exist and broke every launch.|(Save states) Not supported. Xenia has no save-state implementation at all, so rewind, run-ahead and netplay are unavailable by design rather than by oversight.|Keyboard analog-stick binds and the menu hotkey are global RetroArch settings, not core-settable."
